# Build artifacts
# `target/` alone matches only a top-level directory — the Rust crate's own
# fraiseql_rs/target/ (21 GB of local dev artifacts) was being copied into the
# build context, which is what made `docker build` run out of disk.
**/target/
dist/
build/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib

# Dependencies
node_modules/
vendor/
.venv/
venv/

# Documentation
docs/
*.md
# Exception: README.md required by maturin (pyproject.toml: readme = "README.md")
!README.md

# Tests
tests/
**/*_test.rs

